implementationPlan.description:
Make SettingsPanel.ts match JetBrains. Edit moe-vscode/src/panels/SettingsPanel.ts and add no import.

(a) Export `effectivePolicyRows(settings: unknown): { label: string; value: string; detail: string }[]`, a pure port of MoeSettingsDialog.effectivePolicyRows. It takes the RAW wire settings, because VS Code does not normalize them the way MoeJson does, and it applies the daemon's readers:
- s is the object when settings is a non-null, non-array object, else {};
- autoCommit, checkpointCommits, checkpointPush and commitBoardState are on unless they are exactly false; commitHooks is on only when exactly true (getCommitScope.ts);
- consolidationBranch and qualityGate count only when they are strings, trimmed, else '' (wrapper isinstance(v, str), complete_task typeof);
- the landing branch is a glob when it contains '*';
- qualityGateScope 'everyTask' means every task; anything else means epic-final only;
- attribution.undeclared is read only from a plain-object attribution: 'never', 'always', or anything else as solo;
- each taskSizing threshold must be an integer number above 0 (planSize.ts positiveInt), else defaults 8/12/5/10, and each max is lifted to its warn value.
Copy every label, value and detail string verbatim from MoeSettingsDialog.kt; the corpus pins them.

(b) Export SETTINGS_BUNDLE_TEXT, holding the four bundle texts in plain form (the 'Landing & Gate Policy (read-only)' title, the read-only hint, the 'Enable Agent Teams (Claude Code workers only)' label and its hint).

(c) In the HTML:
- drop the Git section (autoCreateBranch, branchPattern, commitPattern);
- add an enableAgentTeams checkbox under Agent, checked only when settings.enableAgentTeams === true, with the bundle label and hint;
- add `<h2>` with the title, then `<section id="landingPolicy">` holding one `<div class="policy-row">` per row: `<span class="policy-label">`, `<span class="policy-value">`, and `<div class="policy-detail">` only when the detail is non-empty, each value through escapeHtml; then the hint. No form control goes inside the section.

(d) The save handler builds exactly {approvalMode, speedModeDelayMs, agentCommand, enableAgentTeams: message.enableAgentTeams === true} and nothing else, matching JetBrains MoeCommandSender.updateSettings.

Error handling: effectivePolicyRows never throws on any JSON shape. Wrong types fall back to the daemon defaults, because project.json is hand-editable. The save path keeps its existing not-connected warning and its catch.

Re-run the corpus test in place: C1 to C3 pass.
